{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 12, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "**A Whirlwind Trip to Japan**\n\nLast month, I finally embarked on my dream journey to Japan, a country where tradition and innovation coexist seamlessly. My adventure began in Tokyo, where neon lights and ancient temples collided. I sipped matcha at a serene tea house in Asakusa, then boarded the Shinkansen to Kyoto, the heart of traditional Japan.\n\nKyoto’s bamboo forests and golden temples left me in awe. Fushimi Inari’s endless torii gates and the peaceful Kinkaku-ji (Golden Pavilion) felt like stepping into a painting. I tried my hand at a tea ceremony—clumsy but memorable—and devoured kaiseki, a multi-course meal that was pure art.\n\nOsaka’s street food stalls in Dotonbori were a highlight. Takoyaki and okonomiyaki burst with flavor, and the energy was infectious. I even braved the bullet train to Hiroshima, where history unfolded at the Peace Memorial Park. The atomic bomb dome’s haunting silence spoke volumes.\n\nBack in Tokyo, I explored Shibuya’s chaotic charm and the quiet elegance of Meiji Shrine. A sushi-making class in Tsukiji Market topped it off—though my rolls were far from perfect, the chef’s patience was heartwarming.\n\nJapan’s blend of precision, beauty, and warmth made this trip unforgettable. From the bullet train’s punctuality to the cherry blossoms’ fleeting beauty, every moment was magic. I left with a suitcase full of souvenirs and a heart full of memories—already planning my return.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.059999264776706696}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.07038097828626633}, {"token": " Wh", "logprob": -0.35210058093070984}, {"token": "irl", "logprob": -8.34461570775602e-06}, {"token": "wind", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -1.0901193618774414}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -0.020727338269352913}, {"token": " Japan", "logprob": -0.00360802817158401}, {"token": "**\n\n", "logpro